    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>Catching a whiff of your own wrist at lunchtime and realising your scent has completely abandoned you is a uniquely modern irritation. You put it on at 8am, and by 1pm you might as well have bathed in tap water. The natural assumption is that the fragrance is poor quality. In almost every case, that is not what is happening.</p><p>Fragrance longevity is governed by skin chemistry, moisture levels, and evaporation physics. Here is the science of why scent disappears and how to ensure your perfume stays with you all day.</p>"
      }
    },
